caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/ModalTemplate
title: ModalTemplate

! Summary
Add a section to the new-item modal.

! Detail
Tag a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/ModalTemplate` (plus exactly one `$:/tags/hypergsd/ModalTemplate/Portion/N`, `/Portion/Top` or `/Portion/Full` tag) to make it a modal attribute section. Variables in scope:

| !Variable | !Meaning |
|new-temp |The working temp tiddler (`$:/temp/gsd-new-temp`) — read/write values here |
|new-state |The internal state temp (`$:/temp/gsd-new-state`: selected type, status pick, per-type memory) |
|current-type |Currently selected type name |
|section-target / section-type / section-mode / section-status-target |The chassis contract the panel sets too — dual-context sections (ui/attributes) read these instead of assuming `currentTiddler`; here `section-target` is the data temp and `section-mode` is `modal` |
|gsd-* |The invoking button's parameters |

Write user selections to fields on `new-temp` (the submit step maps them onto the created tiddler); the Type selector lives on its `hgsd-type` field.

```
title: $:/plugins/MyPlugin/ui/modal/due-date
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

<label>Due date:
<$edit-text tiddler=<<new-temp>> field="myplugin-due" placeholder="YYYY-MM-DD"/>
</label>
```

Sections are visibility-gated per `$:/config/hypergsdModal/visibility/<section>` (default show).

! Best Practice
Respect the selected type — gate on `<current-type>` rather than assuming an action.